  "status": "implemented, independently reviewed, scoped validation complete",
  "contract": [
    "One host-only native-turn lifetime surrounds main and child turns, including OFF. Configured connector identity, client generation, policy epoch and exact arguments are asserted at actual stdio/HTTP/SSE dispatch and after response.",
    "Unknown MCP services gain no private-reference restoration authority. Ordinary no-reference arguments retain their bytes. A post-dispatch identity change returns only an executed/withheld receipt and never replays business work.",
    "One read-tier mcp_resource entry lists resources/templates and reads only bounded, expiring, turn-owned handles/cursors. Templates confer no arbitrary URI authority; binary resources are refused. Updates retain only fixed metadata and drain at the existing shared result encoder.",
    "Subscriptions end with the native turn; local capabilities/listeners always retire. A fixed old-connection unsubscribe is best effort, not a claim that a remote server acknowledged teardown.",
    "A shared availability predicate excludes this new native-turn-only tool from CLI schemas and adaptive discovery. Direct/proxy guessed names are refused; existing CLI/local tools remain unchanged.",
    "The URL detector uses JSON syntax boundaries only for the automatic lexical wrapper scan. Raw and decoded URL credential detection and explicit rules retain their original coverage."
  ],
  "independentReview": {
    "reviewers": [
      "m2_bot_delivery",
      "m2_consumer_review",
      "root (design and additional source review)"
    ],
    "findingsResolved": [
      "Retain possibly accepted subscriptions and separate exact old-connection teardown authority from obsolete policy/config guards.",
      "Revalidate exact handle membership/expiry after preparation and at actual dispatch, including list_changed before the first subscription.",
      "Prevent a resource URI and adjacent JSON email field from forming a false URL-password match across JSON syntax.",
      "Do not advertise native-turn resource handles to a CLI process without the required turn context."
    ],
    "notes": [
